# An Appeal to Pandit Nehru
Tamil title: பண்டிதருக்கு வேண்டுகோள்

Declaring, "The whole of South India opposes Hindi. This is not a minority calculated merely by numbers; it is the opposition expressed by one entire region of the country," all those listed below signed and sent an appeal to Pandit Nehru asking that Hindi be abandoned.

The South will certainly honour their love of Tamil and their concern that the country's future should not be surrounded by danger. Whatever answer Delhi may give, the Tamil language owes its gratitude to all these people for uniting over a worthy issue and taking action without dismissing it merely because it was something we had already said.

The public-spirited signatories to the statement were:

1. C. P. Ramaswami Iyer, former Vice-Chancellor of Annamalai and Banaras Hindu Universities
2. K. Srinivasan, Editor, *The Hindu*
3. T. M. Krishnaswami Iyer, former Chief Justice of the Travancore State High Court
4. C. Rajagopalachari, former Governor-General
5. S. G. Manavala Ramanujam, former Vice-Chancellor of Annamalai University
6. S. Anantharamakrishnan, prominent industrialist
7. R. V. Krishna Iyer, former Secretary of the Madras Legislative Assembly
8. C. R. Srinivasan, Editor, *Swadesamitran*
9. A. N. Sivaraman, Editor, *Dinamani*
10. S. P. Adithan, Editor, *Dina Thanthi*
11. S. S. Vasan, Editor, *Ananda Vikatan*
12. T. Sadasivam, Editor, *Kalki*
13. Khasa Subba Rau, Editor, *Swarajya*
14. V. L. Ethiraj, President of the Bar Association
15. V. C. Gopalratnam, President of the Bar Association
16. M. S. A. Majeed, Honorary Secretary, South Indian Muslim Educational Association
17. M. Subbaraya Iyer, Correspondent, Vivekananda College and the Madras Institute of Technology
18. R. Krishnamurti, Principal, Pachaiyappa's College
19. M. K. Shanmugam, Principal, Sir Theagaraya College
20. R. P. Sethu Pillai, Professor of Tamil, University of Madras
21. M. M. Bhatt, Professor of Kannada, University of Madras
22. Mrs Rukmini Arundale, Kalakshetra, Adyar
23. Mrs M. S. Subbulakshmi, celebrated musician
24. T. K. Shanmugam, prominent Tamil theatre artist
25. T. K. Bhagavathi, prominent Tamil theatre artist
26. A. G. Venkatachari, President, Tamil Writers' Association
27. S. R. Venkataraman, Secretary, Servants of India Society
28. K. Kothandapani Pillai, Secretary, Tamil Cultural Association
29. A. Subbiah, President, South Indian Affairs Study Forum
30. S. Narayanaswami, Secretary, YMIA
31. P. J. Anantharaj, Secretary, YMCA
32. Mrs L. A. Pithavadian, President, YWCA
33. H. C. Kothari, President, Madras Stock Exchange
34. V. S. L. Nathan, Honorary Secretary, Tamil Chamber of Commerce
35. S. Chellachami, Secretary, Official Language Conference

News item, *Dravida Nadu*, 3 November 1957.

---NOTES---
The OCR badly fragments list numbers but the scans show a continuous list of thirty-five signatories. Names and institutional titles are transliterated conservatively; scan-confirmed corrections are logged separately.
